course: dictionary
lesson: 9143
title: Sneering
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sneering means mocking someone in a way that shows you think they are worthless. A sneering voice, look or remark sounds scornful, not friendly. It is an unkind way to talk.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Checking isn't sneering: Rhys's zoo sign about polar bears is roughly right, and finding that out is part of the game too.» The writer says checking is not sneering. Checking a sign to see if it is right is fair; it is not mocking anyone.
explain: Sneering can work as a verb, a describing word or a noun. He was sneering at us uses the verb sneer. A sneering tone describes a voice. Sneering as a noun means the act of mocking someone in that unkind way.
fact: Sneering means mocking someone and showing you think they are worthless.
fact: Sneering is the -ing form of the verb «sneer»: he was sneering at us.
fact: «Checking isn't sneering» shows that checking whether something is right is not the same as mocking it.
fact: A sneering tone or a sneering remark is unkind, and it counts as unkind words.
fact: Useful phrases: a sneering tone, a sneering remark, sneering at someone.
exercise: The sentence says «Checking isn't sneering». Which of these is sneering? | Checking a sign to see if it is right | Finding out that a zoo sign is roughly right | *Mocking someone as if their work is worthless | Playing a game about polar bears
exercise: Lara says her friend spoke in a sneering tone. What does a sneering tone sound like? | A voice that whispers in the library | A quiet, gentle voice that comforts | A happy, singing voice | *A mocking, scornful voice that shows contempt
exercise: Which of these shows the -ing form of the verb sneer? | a sneering smile | *he was sneering at us | a sneering remark | the sneering crowd
test: Which word best describes a remark that mocks someone and shows they are worthless? | *Sneering | Cheerful | Ancient | Luminous
test: Which sentence uses sneering as a verb? | *The boys were sneering at the new girl. | Her sneering smile looked odd. | The cat was sleeping on the mat. | The sneering remark hurt her feelings.
exam: The sentence «Checking isn't sneering» shows that sneering means what? | *Mocking someone unkindly, not checking that something is right | Smiling happily at a sign | Checking facts very carefully | Shouting loudly at a zoo
